    "q-129149": {
      "dom_id": "step-q129149",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{3}[2f(t)+4g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t$ given that ${\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-3,\\,\\sqrt{2},\\,2⟩$ and ${\\int }_{0}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨-\\frac{3}{2},\\,-\\frac{1}{4},\\,1⟩.$",
      "worked_solution": "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{3}[2f(t)+4g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t=2{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+4{\\int }_{0}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}[2f(t)+4g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =2{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+4{\\int }_{0}^{3}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2⟨-3,\\,\\sqrt{2},\\,2⟩+4⟨-\\frac{3}{2},\\,-\\frac{1}{4},\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-6,\\,2\\sqrt{2},\\,4⟩+⟨-6,\\,-1,\\,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-12,\\,2\\sqrt{2}-1,\\,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-129149-a",
