    "q-32496": {
      "dom_id": "step-q32496",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{1}[6f(t)-2g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t$ given that ${\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,-\\frac{2}{3},\\,3⟩$ and ${\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩.$",
      "worked_solution": "From the vector addition and scalar multiplication rules, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}[6f(t)-2g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t=6{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-2{\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[6f(t)-2g(t)]\\,\\text{d}t & =6{\\int }_{0}^{1}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-2{\\int }_{0}^{1}g(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =6⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,-\\frac{2}{3},\\,3⟩-2⟨1,\\,1,\\,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,\\,-4,\\,18⟩-⟨2,\\,2,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-6,\\,16⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
