    "q-98263": {
      "dom_id": "step-q98263",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Calculate \n${\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$\ngiven that\n${\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨6,\\,-2,\\,-4⟩$\nand\n${\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=⟨3,\\,5,\\,-7⟩.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the adjacent intervals rule, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t+{\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nWe can rearrange the above as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t={\\int }_{0}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nFinally, using the given information, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\cdot {\\int }_{0}^{4}\\frac{1}{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t-{\\int }_{3}^{4}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =2\\cdot ⟨6,\\,-2,\\,-4⟩-⟨3,\\,5,\\,-7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12,\\,-4,\\,-8⟩-⟨3,\\,5,\\,-7⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9,\\,-9,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
