    "q-129296": {
      "dom_id": "step-q129296",
      "name": "Question 16",
      "problem": "Find ${\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=7\\,i-4\\,j-k$ \nand \n$c=3\\,i-5\\,j+2\\,k.$",
      "worked_solution": "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{2}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(3\\,i-5\\,j+2\\,k)\\times (7\\,i-4\\,j-k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -5 & 2 \\\\ 7 & -4 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 2 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 7 & -1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}3 & -5 \\\\ 7 & -4\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(5+8)i-(-3-14)j+(-12+35)k \\\\  & =13\\,i+17\\,j+23\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
