    "q-129295": {
      "dom_id": "step-q129295",
      "name": "Question 19",
      "problem": "Find ${\\int }_{0}^{3}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=i+j-3\\,k$ \nand \n$c=i-j+2\\,k.$",
      "worked_solution": "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{3}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{0}^{3}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(i-j+2\\,k)\\times (i+j-3\\,k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(3-2)i-(-3-2)j+(1+1)k \\\\  & =i+5\\,j+2\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
