      "name": "Question 20",
      "problem": "Find ${\\int }_{1}^{5}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t$ \ngiven that \n${\\int }_{1}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=i-j+3\\,k$ \nand \n$c=2\\,i-k.$",
      "worked_solution": "The cross-product rule states that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{1}^{5}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t=c\\times {\\int }_{1}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\n \n\nApplying the cross-product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{5}c\\times f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =c\\times {\\int }_{1}^{5}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =(2\\,i-k)\\times (i-j+3\\,k) \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =(0-1)i-(6+1)j+(-2-0)k \\\\  & =-i-7\\,j-2\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
